Package: nmaFlow
Type: Package
Title: Integrated Workflows for Network Meta-Analysis
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Walter Esfrain", "Pereira", email = "walter@cca.ufpb.br",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1085-0191")),
    person("Magali Haidee", "Pereira Martinez", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0009-5419-959X"))
    )
Description: A design-aware and teaching-oriented integration layer for network
    meta-analysis. It standardizes arm-level, contrast-level, individual and
    mixed-format evidence; audits and repairs data architecture without silently
    altering scientific treatment definitions; diagnoses network geometry and
    transitivity; orchestrates frequentist, Bayesian, bootstrap, dose-response,
    time-course, component, multivariate, IPD and cross-design workflows; and
    produces publication-ready tables, figures and reproducible reports. Core
    functionality remains R-only, while heavy statistical engines and Python or
    Julia interoperability are optional.
